B.amo=new A.hK(B.aj,"The Sun is the chart's core: not one planet among many but the organizing center everything else orbits, astrologically as well as physically. It describes fundamental identity, purpose, and the quality of life-force a person expresses when simply being most fully themselves.","Identity, vitality, purpose, ego, self-expression, and will.","Associated across cultures with kingship, divinity, and life-giving light \u2014 the visible source without which nothing else in the chart would be seen at all.","Rules Leo.","In fire signs the Sun burns visibly and expressively; in earth signs it expresses identity through tangible achievement and reliability; in air signs through ideas, connection, and social identity; in water signs through feeling, intuition, and emotional depth rather than outward display.","A highly public, identity-defining placement \u2014 Sun in an angular house often makes purpose and selfhood a visible, central life theme rather than a private undercurrent.","Identity expressed through building and stabilizing something \u2014 resources, creativity, shared intimacy, or community, depending on the specific succedent house.","Identity expressed more through process than through a fixed public role \u2014 learning, service, philosophy, or inner life, depending on the specific cadent house.","Trines and sextiles to the Sun tend to bring ease, confidence, and natural support for self-expression from whatever the other planet represents.","Squares and oppositions to the Sun often show friction between core identity and whatever the other planet demands \u2014 real growth usually comes from integrating rather than suppressing either side.",'A conjunction to the Sun blends that planet\'s themes directly into core identity \u2014 often intensifying it, sometimes to the point of the other planet feeling "used up" by how strongly the Sun expresses it.',null,"The Sun's yearly transit through the signs marks the seasonal zodiac calendar itself; its transits to natal points highlight that placement for a short, personally significant window once a year (including, at the Solar Return, the birthday itself).")
B.amk=new A.hK(B.ay,"The Moon governs the inner, instinctive, and emotional self: the reactions that happen before conscious thought catches up, and the conditions under which a person actually feels safe.","Emotion, instinct, habit, nurturing, memory, and comfort.","Tied across traditions to motherhood, the tides, and cyclical renewal \u2014 reflecting rather than generating light, much as mood reflects underlying need.","Rules Cancer.","In fire signs emotional reactions come fast and openly; in earth signs comfort comes through routine and material security; in air signs through conversation and mental processing; in water signs (its natural home) with the most direct, unfiltered emotional depth.","Emotional life becomes a visible, central part of identity or public role \u2014 moods and instincts are less hidden than average.","Emotional security tied closely to resources, creative expression, intimacy, or community, depending on the house.","Emotional life processed more privately \u2014 through learning, daily routine, belief, or solitude, depending on the house.","Trines and sextiles to the Moon bring emotional ease and instinctive support from whatever the other planet represents.","Squares and oppositions to the Moon often show tension between emotional needs and whatever the other planet demands, sometimes surfacing as moodiness until the underlying need is addressed directly.","A conjunction to the Moon blends that planet's themes into instinctive emotional response \u2014 the other planet's energy is felt, not just thought.",null,"The Moon moves fastest of all bodies, transiting the whole zodiac in about a month \u2014 its transits are short, mood-coloring windows rather than long developments, which is why the Daily Card treats the Moon's current sign and phase as a key daily ingredient.")
B.aml=new A.hK(B.bu,"Mercury governs the mind in its everyday, functional sense: thinking, talking, learning, and the countless small exchanges of information that make up ordinary communication.","Communication, thought, learning, reasoning, and travel.","Named for the swift messenger god, moving quickly between the planets as its namesake moved between realms \u2014 fitting for the fastest planet in daily sky-watching besides the Moon.","Rules Gemini and Virgo.","In fire signs thinking is quick and impulsive; in earth signs practical and detail-oriented; in air signs (its most natural home) abstract, curious, and socially fluent; in water signs intuitive, feeling-informed, sometimes less linear.","Communication and thinking become a visible, central part of identity or public role \u2014 often shows up as a naturally talkative or intellectually engaged public presence.","Thinking oriented toward practical outcomes \u2014 resources, creative projects, intimate understanding, or shared goals, depending on the house.","Mercury's natural cadent-house comfort zone \u2014 learning, routine information processing, philosophy, or introspection, depending on the house.","Trines and sextiles to Mercury bring mental ease and clear communication in whatever area the other planet represents.","Squares and oppositions to Mercury often show friction between clear thinking and whatever the other planet demands \u2014 miscommunication or overthinking until it's consciously worked through.","A conjunction to Mercury pulls that planet's themes directly into how someone thinks and talks about them \u2014 often quite literally, as a frequent topic of conversation.","Mercury retrograde is astrology's most famous retrograde period, traditionally associated with communication mishaps, travel delays, and technology hiccups \u2014 and, more constructively, as a good window for review, revision, and reconnecting rather than launching something brand new.","Mercury's transits move quickly and mark short windows where communication, information, or short travel around a given life area becomes more active.")
B.amu=new A.hK(B.aQ,"Venus governs attraction, affection, and value: what a person finds beautiful, who and what they're drawn to, and the way they seek harmony in relationships and surroundings alike.","Love, beauty, harmony, values, and pleasure.","Named for the goddess of love and beauty, and traditionally called both the morning and evening star \u2014 fitting for a planet concerned with both romance's dawn and its steadier evening warmth.","Rules Taurus and Libra.","In fire signs love is bold and enthusiastic; in earth signs sensual, loyal, and grounded in tangible affection; in air signs social, intellectual, and idea-driven; in water signs deeply emotional and romantically intuitive.","Charm, aesthetics, and relational warmth become a visible, central part of identity or public role.","Venus's natural succedent-house comfort zone \u2014 values, love, and harmony expressed through resources, creativity, intimacy, or community, depending on the house.","Affection and aesthetic sense expressed more through process than display \u2014 in learning, daily habits, belief, or inner life, depending on the house.","Trines and sextiles to Venus bring ease in love, aesthetics, and social warmth wherever the other planet touches.","Squares and oppositions to Venus often show tension between the desire for harmony and whatever the other planet demands \u2014 sometimes surfacing as people-pleasing until a more honest balance is found.","A conjunction to Venus adds charm, warmth, and aesthetic sensibility to that planet's themes \u2014 often making them easier to enjoy, though sometimes at the cost of being fully honest about them.","Venus retrograde periods are traditionally linked to reevaluating relationships and values \u2014 old flames resurfacing, or a genuine reassessment of what (and who) actually feels worth investing in.","Venus's transits mark windows of heightened social warmth, aesthetic sensitivity, or romantic opportunity around whatever life area it moves through.")
B.amn=new A.hK(B.aV,"Mars governs drive, desire, and assertiveness: the willingness to act, compete, and pursue what is wanted rather than simply hope for it.","Action, desire, courage, conflict, and physical energy.","Named for the god of war, and traditionally read as the more aggressive, combative counterpart to Venus's harmony \u2014 together the classical pairing of attraction and pursuit.","Traditional ruler of Scorpio; modern and traditional ruler of Aries.","In fire signs (its most natural home) action is direct and immediate; in earth signs disciplined and results-focused; in air signs strategic and debate-driven; in water signs intense but more internally held, surfacing through emotional determination rather than open confrontation.","Assertiveness and drive become a visible, central part of identity or public role \u2014 often a genuinely competitive or highly active public presence.","Drive channeled into building something concrete \u2014 resources, creative output, intimacy, or shared goals, depending on the house.","Energy expressed through sustained effort in process rather than a single decisive act \u2014 learning, daily work, belief, or inner struggle, depending on the house.","Trines and sextiles to Mars bring confident, well-directed energy and healthy assertiveness wherever the other planet touches.","Squares and oppositions to Mars often generate real friction or impatience \u2014 genuinely useful when it drives constructive action, genuinely costly when it tips into unchecked conflict.","A conjunction to Mars energizes that planet's themes, often considerably \u2014 adding drive and urgency, for better and for worse.","Mars retrograde periods are traditionally read as a time when direct action doesn't land as expected \u2014 better suited to reassessing strategy and unfinished conflicts than launching a brand-new pursuit.","Mars's transits mark windows of heightened energy, motivation, or friction around whatever life area it moves through \u2014 genuinely good timing for decisive action, if channeled deliberately.")
B.amr=new A.hK(B.bR,"Jupiter governs growth, optimism, and expansion: the impulse to reach further, believe bigger, and trust that things can genuinely get better.","Growth, luck, optimism, wisdom, generosity, and abundance.",'Named for the king of the Roman gods, and traditionally called the "Greater Benefic" \u2014 the largest planet in the sky read, fittingly, as the astrological symbol of largeness itself: of opportunity, faith, and sheer scale.',"Traditional ruler of Pisces; modern and traditional ruler of Sagittarius.","In fire signs (its most natural home) growth is adventurous and confident; in earth signs practical and steadily accumulated; in air signs intellectual and socially expansive; in water signs spiritual, compassionate, and emotionally generous.","Optimism and a sense of expansive possibility become a visible, central part of identity or public role.","Growth channeled into building lasting abundance \u2014 resources, creative work, intimacy, or community, depending on the house.","Jupiter's natural cadent-house comfort zone \u2014 growth through learning, service, philosophy, or inner development, depending on the house.","Trines and sextiles to Jupiter bring luck, generosity, and easy growth wherever the other planet touches \u2014 genuinely one of the more welcome aspect patterns to have.","Squares and oppositions to Jupiter can show overconfidence, excess, or overpromising in whatever the other planet represents \u2014 growth without enough grounding.","A conjunction to Jupiter amplifies that planet's themes considerably, usually for the better, though sometimes past a healthy scale if left unchecked.","Jupiter retrograde periods are traditionally read as a time for internal growth and reflection on belief and opportunity, rather than outward expansion.","Jupiter's roughly year-long transit through each sign marks a broad theme of growth and opportunity for everyone, felt most personally wherever it activates an individual's own placements.")
B.amp=new A.hK(B.b4,"Saturn governs structure, discipline, and time: the boundaries, responsibilities, and long slow effort that eventually produce something durable enough to last.","Discipline, responsibility, limits, mastery, and maturity.",'Named for the god of time and harvest, and traditionally called the "Greater Malefic" not out of malice but because growth here always requires real, sometimes uncomfortable, effort \u2014 the harvest that only comes after patient tending.',"Traditional ruler of Aquarius; modern and traditional ruler of Capricorn.","In fire signs discipline is applied to bold ambition; in earth signs (its most natural home) to practical, tangible achievement; in air signs to structured thinking and long-term planning; in water signs to emotional maturity and the patient tending of lasting bonds.","Responsibility and long-term achievement become a visible, central part of identity or public role \u2014 often a reputation built slowly but built to last.","Discipline applied to building lasting security \u2014 resources, creative mastery, committed intimacy, or long-term community standing, depending on the house.","Structure applied through sustained process \u2014 rigorous learning, consistent daily discipline, firmly held belief, or serious inner work, depending on the house.","Trines and sextiles to Saturn bring steady, earned support and staying power wherever the other planet touches.","Squares and oppositions to Saturn often show real restriction or self-doubt in whatever the other planet represents \u2014 hard, but frequently where the most durable long-term growth eventually comes from.","A conjunction to Saturn adds weight, seriousness, and structure to that planet's themes \u2014 sometimes felt as a limitation at first, often becoming a genuine strength once mastered.","Saturn retrograde periods are traditionally read as a time for reviewing and internally restructuring commitments and responsibilities, rather than taking on entirely new ones.","Saturn's roughly 2.5-year transit through each sign marks a long chapter of tests and consolidation, felt most personally around the Saturn Return (roughly ages 29, 58, and 87) when it returns to its own natal position.")
B.amt=new A.hK(B.cK,"Uranus governs sudden change, independence, and innovation: the impulse to break from convention and the flashes of insight that arrive without warning.","Rebellion, innovation, freedom, sudden change, and originality.",'Named for the primordial sky god and discovered only in 1781, Uranus is read as the first of the modern, slower-moving "generational" planets \u2014 its placement by sign shapes a whole generation more than any one individual.',"Modern ruler of Aquarius (traditionally ruled by Saturn).","In fire signs rebellion is bold and immediate; in earth signs innovation is applied practically, often to systems and institutions; in air signs (its natural home) intellectually radical and socially progressive; in water signs emotionally unpredictable, breaking old patterns of feeling rather than thought.","Independence and unconventionality become a visible, central part of identity or public role.","Sudden change touching resources, creative expression, intimacy, or community \u2014 depending on the house, in ways that resist being settled or predictable.","Innovation expressed through ongoing intellectual or spiritual restlessness \u2014 learning, routine-breaking, belief, or inner insight, depending on the house.","Trines and sextiles to Uranus bring welcome, generally constructive surprises and a comfortable relationship with change wherever the other planet touches.","Squares and oppositions to Uranus often bring disruptive, harder-to-predict upheaval in whatever the other planet represents.","A conjunction to Uranus makes that planet's themes unpredictable and prone to sudden change \u2014 exciting, but rarely stable.","Uranus spends roughly five months of every year retrograde \u2014 traditionally read as a time when change is processed and integrated internally rather than acted out visibly.",'Uranus\'s roughly 7-year transit through each sign marks a generational theme of disruption and innovation, felt personally most around the "Uranus opposition" in midlife (roughly age 40-42) when it opposes its own natal position.')
B.amm=new A.hK(B.cr,"Neptune governs dreams, spirituality, and dissolution of boundaries: imagination, compassion, and the pull toward something larger and less clearly defined than the ordinary material world.","Imagination, spirituality, compassion, illusion, and idealism.","Named for the god of the sea, and read as a planet of fluid, boundary-dissolving depth \u2014 as hard to hold onto directly as water itself, for better (transcendence, art, compassion) and for worse (confusion, escapism, deception).","Modern ruler of Pisces (traditionally ruled by Jupiter).","In fire signs idealism is passionate and visionary; in earth signs imagination is applied practically, often through art or healing work; in air signs expressed intellectually, as idealistic or utopian thinking; in water signs (its natural home) as deep, unfiltered emotional and spiritual sensitivity.","Idealism, imagination, or spiritual sensitivity become a visible, central part of identity or public role.","Dreams and ideals touching resources, creative work, intimacy, or community \u2014 often in ways that resist clean, concrete definition.","Neptune's natural cadent-house comfort zone \u2014 spirituality and imagination expressed through learning, service, belief, or inner life, depending on the house.","Trines and sextiles to Neptune bring inspiration, compassion, and creative flow wherever the other planet touches.","Squares and oppositions to Neptune often bring confusion, idealization, or difficulty seeing whatever the other planet represents clearly \u2014 worth double-checking assumptions rather than trusting the first impression.","A conjunction to Neptune blurs and softens that planet's themes \u2014 beautiful and inspiring at its best, foggy or self-deceiving at its most unchecked.","Neptune spends roughly five months of every year retrograde \u2014 traditionally read as a time when illusions are more likely to be seen through, for better or worse.","Neptune's roughly 14-year transit through each sign marks a generational theme of collective idealism or disillusionment, felt personally in wherever it touches an individual's own placements.")
B.amj=new A.hK(B.ch,"Pluto governs transformation at the deepest level: death and rebirth in the broad sense of anything that must fully end before something truly new can begin, along with the hidden, sometimes uncomfortable truths that power and intimacy both eventually surface.","Transformation, power, intensity, the unconscious, and rebirth.","Named for the god of the underworld, and read \u2014 despite its reclassification as a dwarf planet astronomically \u2014 as a full participant in astrological tradition since its 1930 discovery: the slowest-moving, most generationally-scaled of the outer planets.","Modern ruler of Scorpio (traditionally ruled by Mars).","In fire signs transformation is fought for directly and visibly; in earth signs it reshapes material structures and institutions; in air signs it transforms ideas, communication, and collective thought; in water signs (its natural home) it operates at the deepest emotional and psychological level.","Intensity and personal power become a visible, central part of identity or public role \u2014 often someone who is hard to overlook and slow to fully reveal.","Transformation touching resources, creative work, intimacy, or community \u2014 frequently the house placement most associated with genuinely reshaping a whole area of life rather than merely adjusting it.","Pluto's influence unfolding gradually through process \u2014 learning, service, belief, or the unconscious itself, depending on the house.","Trines and sextiles to Pluto bring the ability to handle intensity and transformation constructively wherever the other planet touches.","Squares and oppositions to Pluto often bring power struggles or compulsive intensity around whatever the other planet represents \u2014 frequently pointing to exactly what most needs to be consciously faced rather than avoided.","A conjunction to Pluto intensifies that planet's themes considerably, often bringing them into contact with real personal power and eventual transformation.","Pluto spends roughly five to six months of every year retrograde \u2014 traditionally read as a time when transformation happens internally, beneath the surface, before it becomes visible.","Pluto's extremely slow transit (well over a decade in each sign) marks generational transformation more than a personal timing tool, felt most personally through its harder aspects to an individual's own placements.")
B.ams=new A.hK(B.hn,"The North Node isn't a planet at all \u2014 it marks the point where the Moon's orbit crosses the ecliptic heading north, one of two mathematical points (with the South Node exactly opposite) rather than a physical body. In Western astrology it's read as a direction of growth: qualities that feel unfamiliar, effortful, or even mildly uncomfortable to develop, precisely because they aren't already second nature.","Growth, destiny, unfamiliar territory, and forward development.","Called Rahu in Vedic astrology, sometimes pictured as a serpent's head swallowing the Sun or Moon during an eclipse \u2014 the nodes mark exactly the points where eclipses can occur, since an eclipse needs the Sun or Moon to be near one of them.",u.r,"In fire signs, growth means learning to act and lead rather than wait; in earth signs, it means building tangible, sustained structure; in air signs, it means engaging ideas and other people more openly; in water signs, it means trusting emotional and intuitive depth rather than staying purely rational.","The growth direction becomes a visible, central life theme \u2014 often something the person actively works toward across their whole adult life, not a background detail.","Growth centered on resources, self-expression, intimacy, or community \u2014 an area steadily built up over time rather than arrived at suddenly.","Growth unfolding through learning, service, belief, or the unconscious \u2014 often less visible from the outside than an angular placement, but no less real.","Trines and sextiles to the North Node mean the growth direction has natural support from wherever the other planet falls \u2014 help that still needs to be used, not automatic success.","Squares and oppositions to the North Node often describe exactly what creates friction with that growth \u2014 frequently the South Node's comfortable, familiar pull competing with it, since the South Node sits opposite by definition.","A conjunction to the North Node ties that planet directly into the chart's growth story \u2014 its themes become part of what the person is actively developing toward.","The nodes always move backward (retrograde) through the zodiac under the Mean Node convention this app uses \u2014 about 3\u2032 of arc per day, completing a full backward circuit in roughly 18.6 years. This is normal, constant motion, not an occasional station the way a planet's retrograde is.","As the nodes slowly regress through the signs (about one sign every year and a half), they mark broad generational and collective growth themes more than fast personal timing \u2014 felt most personally when a transiting node crosses an individual's own placements.")
B.amq=new A.hK(B.ho,"The South Node sits exactly opposite the North Node \u2014 where the Moon's orbit crosses the ecliptic heading south. Where the North Node points toward growth, the South Node describes what already feels familiar and innate: strengths carried in almost too easily, which can become a comfort zone that's worth stepping out of rather than a destination in itself.","Familiarity, innate ability, comfort zones, and what to release.","Called Ketu in Vedic astrology, traditionally pictured as a serpent's tail \u2014 the counterpart to Rahu/the North Node's head. Both nodes together mark the two points where eclipses occur.",u.r,"In fire signs, the comfort zone is bold action without much reflection; in earth signs, it's material security and routine; in air signs, it's detached analysis over felt experience; in water signs, it's emotional withdrawal into what's already known.","The familiar, innate quality is front and center \u2014 often an early, easy strength that the person is nonetheless encouraged to balance rather than lean on exclusively.","Comfort and innate ability centered on resources, self-expression, intimacy, or community \u2014 areas that come easily without necessarily being where the chart's growth is pointed.","A familiar, well-worn pattern in learning, service, belief, or the unconscious \u2014 often something to hold loosely rather than retreat into.","Trines and sextiles to the South Node describe an easy, natural flow with whatever the other planet touches \u2014 genuinely useful, but worth pairing with active North Node development rather than relied on alone.","Squares and oppositions to the South Node highlight tension between old, familiar patterns and other parts of the chart \u2014 often the same friction described from the North Node's side, since the two nodes are always exactly opposite.","A conjunction to the South Node pulls that planet toward familiar, well-practiced territory \u2014 comfortable, but worth watching so it doesn't crowd out the North Node's growth direction.","Like the North Node, the South Node always moves backward (retrograde) through the zodiac under the Mean Node convention this app uses \u2014 constant motion, not an occasional station.","As the nodes slowly regress through the signs, a transiting South Node crossing an individual's own placements often coincides with periods of release or letting go of something familiar, mirroring the North Node's growth-focused transits from the opposite side.")
B.ami=new A.hK(B.hp,"Chiron orbits between Saturn and Uranus, and is read astrologically as bridging structure (Saturn) and awakening (Uranus): the area of life holding a deep, often long-standing wound, and \u2014 with real work \u2014 the same area's eventual capacity to help others heal from something similar.","The wounded healer, deep sensitivity, and hard-won wisdom.","Named for the centaur Chiron, a legendary healer who \u2014 unlike other centaurs in Greek myth \u2014 was wise and gentle, yet carried an incurable wound of his own. Discovered in 1977, orbiting mostly between Saturn and Uranus, which is exactly why it's read as a bridge between the two.","No traditional rulership (discovered too recently), and no widely agreed-upon modern rulership either \u2014 occasionally associated with Virgo or Sagittarius by some modern astrologers, but this isn't a standardized assignment the way Pluto/Scorpio or Uranus/Aquarius are.","In fire signs the wound often centers on identity or confidence; in earth signs, on security or the body; in air signs, on belonging or being understood; in water signs, on emotional safety or early attachment.","The wound and its eventual healing gift become a visible, central part of life \u2014 often something others can sense even before the person names it themselves.","The wound touches resources, self-worth, intimacy, or community \u2014 frequently becoming an area of real value to others once it's been consciously worked through.","The wound plays out more internally, through learning, service, belief, or the unconscious \u2014 often less visible from the outside, but still shaping how the person relates to healing in general.","Trines and sextiles to Chiron mean the healing process has natural support from wherever the other planet falls \u2014 an easier path toward turning the wound into wisdom.","Squares and oppositions to Chiron often bring the wound into active friction with whatever the other planet represents \u2014 painful when triggered, but frequently where the most meaningful growth ends up happening.","A conjunction to Chiron ties that planet's themes directly to the wound \u2014 that part of the personality is where the sensitivity and the eventual healing gift are both most concentrated.","Chiron spends a large part of most years retrograde (its exact orbit is fast and irregular near perihelion, more Saturn-like near aphelion) \u2014 traditionally read as a period when healing work happens internally, revisiting old wounds privately before any outward change.","Chiron's roughly 50-year orbit means a transit through any one sign can last several years, often coinciding with a sustained season of confronting and working through whatever theme that sign represents.")
B.oa=new A.by([B.aj,B.amo,B.ay,B.amk,B.bu,B.aml,B.aQ,B.amu,B.aV,B.amn,B.bR,B.amr,B.b4,B.amp,B.cK,B.amt,B.cr,B.amm,B.ch,B.amj,B.hn,B.ams,B.ho,B.amq,B.hp,B.ami],A.a8("by<dp,hK>"))
B.ajm=new A.by([B.eX,"merge into a single, focused theme",B.eY,"offer a quiet opportunity, if you reach for it",B.eZ,"create friction that, worked with honestly, becomes real growth",B.f_,"flow together with unusual ease",B.f0,"pull in two directions, asking for balance rather than a winner"],t.U2)
B.HJ=new A.hb(B.bu,B.ay,"Mercury conjunct Moon blends thinking and feeling closely \u2014 emotions get put into words easily and quickly, though sometimes before they've been fully processed.",!1)
B.HN=new A.hb(B.aj,B.aQ,"Sun conjunct Venus (astronomically, these two are never far apart) fuses identity closely with charm, aesthetics, and the desire to be liked \u2014 warmth becomes a core part of how someone presents themselves.",!1)
B.HF=new A.hb(B.aV,B.ch,"Mars conjunct Pluto fuses ordinary drive with real intensity \u2014 a formidable combination of willpower, though one that benefits from a conscious outlet rather than being left to simmer.",!1)
B.a00=s([B.HJ,B.HN,B.HF],t.On)
B.HT=new A.qa(B.eX,"A conjunction happens when two points sit at (or very near) the same ecliptic degree \u2014 the closest and most concentrated aspect, blending both planets' energies into a single, hard-to-separate combined force. It is not inherently harmonious or difficult; the blend is simply intense, and its quality depends heavily on which two planets are involved.","A natal conjunction fuses two planetary themes into one persistent personality trait \u2014 the two planets tend to act together automatically, for better or worse, rather than as separable influences a person can easily distinguish in themselves.","A transiting conjunction to a natal point marks a short window where that placement is directly activated and intensified \u2014 often the start of a new cycle involving whatever that natal point represents.",'Because a conjunction blends rather than balances, the most useful question is usually "which of these two energies is currently running the show, and does the other one need more conscious room?"',B.a00)
B.HK=new A.hb(B.aQ,B.aV,"Venus sextile Mars supports easy, healthy chemistry between affection and drive \u2014 attraction and pursuit work well together without much friction.",!1)
B.HL=new A.hb(B.bu,B.bR,"Mercury sextile Jupiter supports optimistic, big-picture thinking that's still reasonably grounded \u2014 a good combination for teaching, writing, or planning.",!1)
B.a77=s([B.HK,B.HL],t.On)
B.HU=new A.qa(B.eY,"A sextile is a 60\xb0 angle, traditionally read as a harmonious, gently supportive aspect \u2014 easier and more available than a trine, but requiring a bit more active choice to use well rather than arriving as effortlessly.","A natal sextile shows a talent or supportive resource between two planets that works well once engaged \u2014 it rarely causes problems on its own, but also rarely insists on being used the way a square or conjunction might.","A transiting sextile to a natal point offers a supportive, low-friction window to make progress on that placement's themes \u2014 a good moment to take a small deliberate step rather than wait for the opportunity to knock harder.","Because sextiles are gentle rather than insistent, they reward active follow-through \u2014 noticing the opportunity and actually taking it, rather than assuming it will happen on its own.",B.a77)
B.HP=new A.hb(B.aV,B.b4,"Mars square Saturn pits drive against restriction \u2014 frustrating when action feels blocked, but capable of producing real discipline and staying power once the friction is channeled rather than fought.",!1)
B.HE=new A.hb(B.aj,B.ay,"Sun square Moon (common near a chart's first-quarter-Moon-like configurations) shows tension between conscious identity and instinctive emotional needs \u2014 integrating both, rather than favoring one, is the long-term work.",!1)
B.HQ=new A.hb(B.aQ,B.ch,"Venus square Pluto brings intensity and possessiveness into love and value \u2014 capable of deep, transformative bonds, but prone to power struggles if trust isn't consciously built.",!1)
B.QD=s([B.HP,B.HE,B.HQ],t.On)
B.HW=new A.qa(B.eZ,"A square is a 90\xb0 angle, traditionally read as a challenging, friction-generating aspect \u2014 the two planets involved want genuinely different things, and that tension has to be actively worked with rather than ignored.","A natal square shows an internal tension between two placements that tends to recur throughout life until it's consciously addressed \u2014 often a source of real personal growth precisely because it can't simply be avoided.","A transiting square to a natal point marks a pressured window where that placement's themes are actively tested \u2014 uncomfortable in the moment, but often when real, lasting change actually gets made.","Squares respond best to direct, conscious engagement \u2014 naming the tension explicitly and choosing a constructive outlet for it tends to work far better than hoping the friction quietly resolves itself.",B.QD)
B.HR=new A.hb(B.aQ,B.bR,"Venus trine Jupiter brings natural warmth, generosity, and good fortune in love and finances \u2014 genuinely one of the more universally pleasant aspects to have.",!1)
B.HM=new A.hb(B.ay,B.cr,"Moon trine Neptune brings easy emotional sensitivity, compassion, and imagination \u2014 a natural gift for empathy and creative or spiritual insight.",!1)
B.HO=new A.hb(B.aj,B.b4,"Sun trine Saturn brings natural discipline and reliability to core identity \u2014 steady follow-through that others tend to trust without needing to be convinced of it.",!1)
B.Xt=s([B.HR,B.HM,B.HO],t.On)
B.HS=new A.qa(B.f_,"A trine is a 120\xb0 angle, traditionally read as the most effortlessly harmonious aspect \u2014 the two planets involved naturally support and understand each other, often to the point that the talent involved is used without much conscious effort at all.","A natal trine shows an area of natural ease or talent between two placements \u2014 genuinely valuable, though sometimes so effortless it goes underdeveloped simply because it never demanded attention the way a harder aspect would.","A transiting trine to a natal point offers a smooth, supportive window for that placement's themes \u2014 good timing, low friction, and worth actively using rather than merely enjoying passively.","Because trines come easily, the main risk is complacency \u2014 deliberately investing effort in a trine's natural talent usually pays off far more than letting it coast.",B.Xt)
B.HG=new A.hb(B.b4,B.aj,'A transiting Saturn opposite natal Sun is one of astrology\'s classic "reality check" transits \u2014 a pressured but valuable window for testing whether current commitments and self-image actually hold up under real responsibility.',!0)
B.HI=new A.hb(B.aQ,B.aV,"Venus opposite Mars highlights the push and pull between wanting harmony and wanting to assert desire directly \u2014 common in dynamic, magnetic partnerships that still need active balancing to avoid a push-pull pattern.",!1)
B.HH=new A.hb(B.ay,B.b4,"Moon opposite Saturn shows tension between emotional needs and self-discipline or duty \u2014 often felt as loneliness until both sides (feeling and structure) are given real, conscious room.",!1)
B.TH=s([B.HG,B.HI,B.HH],t.On)
B.HV=new A.qa(B.f0,"An opposition is a 180\xb0 angle, traditionally read as a challenging aspect of balance and awareness \u2014 the two planets pull toward opposite poles, and the real work is integrating both rather than collapsing into just one side.","A natal opposition often shows up first as a tension projected onto other people or outer circumstances (relationships are a common stage for it) before it's recognized as an internal polarity that needs balancing within the individual themselves.","A transiting opposition to a natal point marks a window where that placement's themes are directly confronted, often through an external situation or person that forces a choice or a genuine reckoning.","Oppositions respond best to deliberately honoring both ends rather than picking a side \u2014 the goal is a working balance, not a winner.",B.TH)
